## 4. Findings (tree: c401adae + adversary file)

| id | file:line | verdict | origin | severity | what was measured | what reaches it |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| F1 | crates/ekr/src/cli/view.rs:65 | confirmed | introduced | medium | one client announcing a >1024-byte body and not sending it blocks every other client (case 1) | any process on the host that can reach 127.0.0.1:<port>, i.e. every local user of a shared machine; browsers send whole bodies, so not a web page |
| F2 | crates/ekr/src/cli/view.rs:65 | confirmed | introduced | medium | one request with `Content-Length: usize::MAX` ends `ekr view` with exit 101, capacity-overflow panic (case 2, probe) | same as F1: any local client, one request, no body needed |
| F3 | crates/ekr/src/cli/view.rs:63 | confirmed | introduced | medium | `Host` is never checked; projection (and evidence) served to `Host: rebound.example` (case 3) | a web page in a browser on the same machine via DNS rebinding, when the port is known (`docs/cli.md` example `--port 8080`; `--port 0` is random but scannable). The story puts authentication out of scope "(loopback only)"; this is the case where loopback-only does not hold |
| F4 | crates/ekr/src/cli/view.rs:22 | confirmed | introduced | low | tiny_http's own 400 (and 408/417/505) carry no nosniff; module doc and docs/cli.md say "every response" (case 4) | any malformed request; body is empty, so doc drift, not an exposure |

Fix names (not applied): F1/F2 - compute the `Reply` on the runtime thread, then move the `Request` into a short-lived thread to `respond` and drop, so the drain and its panic stay off the serving thread (or refuse and close requests with a body before responding). F3 - answer 421/403 unless `Host` is `127.0.0.1:<port>` or `localhost:<port>`. F4 - narrow the doc to "every response the viewer writes".

## 5. Attacked, not broken

- Traversal / encoded ids: `/evidence/..%2f..%2fetc`, `/evidence/a/b`, absolute-form target -> 404, text/plain, nosniff.
- Revisions: `u64::MAX` -> 404 `RevisionNotFound`; `-1`, `x`, duplicate -> 400; `+0` and `00` accepted as revision 0 (same as clap's u64 parse for `--at`; not raised).
- HEAD / OPTIONS on known paths -> 405 with `Allow: GET`; `OPTIONS *` and `POST /nope` -> 404.
- `/?revision=<script>`: page reads it via URLSearchParams + encodeURIComponent, writes only through textContent; meta CSP `default-src 'none'; connect-src 'self'`; no untrusted HTML path found.
- UTF-8 HTML evidence -> text/plain + nosniff; no cookie/CORS header on any handler response.
- Mutants not executed (load average 31 on the shared host; a scratch workspace copy would need a full build). By inspection the suite would miss: method check moved before routing (`POST /elsewhere` 405 instead of 404), dropping `Allow: GET`, dropping `Cache-Control: no-store`.

